Subject: [PATCH] crypto: sun8i-ce: decode V851S CE 2.3 flow interrupts
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [V851S-specific Crypto Engine 2.3 support]

The V851S CE 2.3 interrupt status register allocates two status bits per
flow. The upstream sun8i-ce handler assumes one bit per flow, so it misses
completion interrupts for these requests and waits until timeout. Decode and
acknowledge the two-bit status field for each flow on this variant. The
interrupt control register remains one enable bit per flow.

---
 drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
@@ -307,8 +307,13 @@ static irqreturn_t ce_irq_handler(int irq, void *data)
 	p = readl(ce->base + CE_ISR);
 	for (flow = 0; flow < MAXFLOW; flow++) {
-		if (p & (BIT(flow))) {
-			writel(BIT(flow), ce->base + CE_ISR);
+		u32 flow_status;
+		u32 flow_mask;
+
+		flow_mask = sun8i_ce_is_v23(ce) ? 0x3 << (flow * 2) : BIT(flow);
+		flow_status = p & flow_mask;
+		if (flow_status) {
+			writel(flow_mask, ce->base + CE_ISR);
 			ce->chanlist[flow].status = 1;
 			complete(&ce->chanlist[flow].complete);
 		}
 	}
-- 
2.51.0
